      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T22:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, `SdkLibrary` already implements `DexpreopterInterface` as it extends `java.Library`. However, we cannot call `sdkLib.dexpreopter` as this change delegates the dexpreopting to the `implLibraryModule` and the top level sdk library itself does not perform any dexpreopting anymore.\n\nAnother attempt I have done was `sdkLib.dexpreopter.builtInstalledForApex \u003d sdkLib.implLibraryModule.dexpreopter.builtInstalledForApex`, but that led to other errors in androidmk.\n\nI believe that this special casing can go away once we start listing the impl libraries in the bootclasspath_fragments and systemserver_fragments, as the sdk_library modules listed here end up in the apexes.",
