      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T22:00:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would this treat a java library dependency to be in the same apex if users specify the .impl library explicitly in their Android.bp file?\n\n\n```\n# hypothetical example\njava_sdk_library {\n   name: \"framework-bluetooth\",\n   libs: [\"framework-wifi.impl\"],\n}\n```\n\nAfter this CL, would `DepIsInSameApex` return true on `framework-wifi` when called from `framework-bluetooth`\u0027s context?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2225,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2227,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "c817a9711175edee77d2be4c3b209f0afe453264",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67e899c9_81ad13e7",
        "filename": "java/sdk_library.go",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 2227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T22:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nope, this change only makes the impl library of a sdk library to be considered as to be in a same apex with the sdk library that generates the impl library. i.e. in the above example, `framework-bluetooth` and `framework-bluetooth.impl` would be considered to be in the same apex, not with `framework-wifi.impl`.\n\n`module.implLibraryModuleName()` returns the [string with \".impl\" suffix appended to the module name](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/sdk_library.go;drc\u003d00e0991f702751098fe95c0dfce5cd3725659abf;l\u003d1000).",
